#!/usr/bin/env python3
# D2a2: wall-jet enthalpy closure, surface_patch.jet_closure = enthalpy.
# T_gas(r) is marched outward from the stagnation temperature T_stag (free-jet
# centreline decay phi = min(1, jet_core_length*jet_D/s_c) by default); each
# radial bin (width jet_dr) takes its face absorption
# sum max(0, h*(T_gas - T_s))*dx*dy out of the jet.
#
# Inputs:
#   input_strip    320 x 1 x 4 strip, dx = 0.25 mm, r = 0-80 mm, one step from
#                  a uniform 500 K IC, cell form, no losses; h = 5000*min(1,
#                  0.02/r) carries the annulus weight 2*pi*r/dy. s_c = 50 mm,
#                  phi = 0.75, T_stag = 1198.2875 K; continuous march: core
#                  exp(-pi r^2 h_ref/(m cp)), then exp(-(r - r_core)/L),
#                  L = 19.89 mm.
#   input_quarter  24 x 24 x 40 drilling quarter disk at 2 mm, pinned, 30 s.
#   ../robin_jet/input_jet   the D2a expression column.
# Runs (1 rank unless noted):
#   N0, N1  robin_jet stand-off run (its B case, 10 s); N1 adds jet_closure = none
#   B4 B2 B1 B05   strip at jet_dr = 4, 2, 1, 0.5 mm (decay, nozzle mass)
#   B1e, B1n       B1 with jet_entrained_mass = 1 / jet_stagnation = nozzle
#   B3             B1 on 3 ranks
#   G, Gbug  strip with the axis inside it (x0 = 20 mm), jet_stagnation =
#            nozzle, h = 100/max(0.02, r) and the AMReX-trap order
#            h = 100/max(r, 0.02)
#   E, Eon   strip with losses on; E has the nozzle 4 mm BELOW the top
#            (s < 0 everywhere, collision radius 0), Eon 50 mm above
#   Q, Qh    quarter disk (decay) at jet_dr = 2 mm (default) and 1 mm;
#   Q3       Q on 3 ranks;  QN, QE  Q with nozzle / entrained mass, 10 s
#   QF       quarter disk with a descending nozzle (30 mm above the top,
#            1 mm/s, collision radius 10 mm, 45 s): phi = 1 at the start, the
#            outer top ends above the nozzle plane
#   P1-P3    parse aborts: T_flame_expr under enthalpy; enthalpy on the C1
#            constants input (../robin_pinned/input_pinned, no h_expr); a bad
#            jet_stagnation value
# Checks:
#   (a) N1 == N0: Level_0 Cell_D, removal_events.csv, whole thermo.dat text;
#       neither has a jet_* column; Q's last eight columns are the jet_* set.
#   (b) Strip: T_gas per column from the step's top-cell rise (cell form:
#       dT = dt*h*(T_gas - 500)/(dz*rho*Cp)) equals the discrete march
#       (excess *= 1 - 2 pi h_ref min(r_mid, r_core) dr/(m cp) per bin) to 1e-9,
#       for B4-B05, B1e (m = mdot/phi) and B1n (T_stag = T_nozzle); against
#       the continuous solution at each bin's inner edge (r <= r_core + 3 L)
#       the error falls with jet_dr at first order (each halving: ratio
#       1.8-2.2) and is <= 5 % at 0.5 mm; jet_T_exhaust matches the recursion
#       to print precision; the jet_profile.csv row per bin carries the
#       recursion's inlet T_gas (1e-12) and its P_share sums to jet_P_face.
#   (c) Every row of every enthalpy run (6-digit print, 1e-5; ALAMO aborts at
#       1e-9): jet_P_face + jet_P_exhaust == jet_P_cap, jet_P_face <= jet_P_cap,
#       jet_P_face + jet_P_exhaust + jet_P_decay == jet_mdot*cp*(T_nozzle -
#       T_ent); jet_P_decay == 0 for nozzle / entrained-mass runs.
#   (c2) jet_T_stag == T_ent + (T_nozzle - T_ent)*min(1, 5 D/jet_s_c) on every
#       row (T_nozzle for jet_stagnation = nozzle); QF has rows on both sides of
#       s_c = 5 D.
#   (d) Q vs Qh: ROP (cumulative h_applied fit, 15-30 s) of the centre column
#       and of the reference column (10, 10) at r = 29.7 mm; |change| <= 2 %.
#   (e) E: jet_P_face = patch_P_robin = 0, jet_T_exhaust = jet_T_stag =
#       jet_T_nozzle (no column marches, s_c = 0), every top cell cools by
#       exactly the cell-form loss; Eon: jet_P_face > 0.
#       QF: completes past the top crossing (30 s), columns with s <= 0 exist
#       at the end, patch_min_standoff > 0.
#   (f) B3 == B1 and Q3 == Q: removal_events.csv, Level_0 FABs (box-index
#       order via Cell_H FabOnDisk), jet_* thermo text; B3 == B1 jet_profile.csv.
#   (g) AMReX parser trap guard: G's jet_P_face equals a numpy replica of the
#       march with h = 100/max(0.02, r) to 1e-5. Gbug is classified against
#       the correct replica and the rewritten one (h = 100*max(r, -0.02)):
#       either is reported (the latter = AMReX 25.12 bug still present);
#       matching neither FAILs.
#   (h) P1-P3 abort with their messages.
#
# Usage: test            (runs ALAMO, then checks)
#        test <outdir>   (checks existing outputs under <outdir>)

